    "type": "text",
    "text": "Lecture 29: linear first order DEs y' + p(x)y = q(x). Set s = 1 for the example y' - 2xy = x, s = 2 for your own p and q (edit them in Coefficients). Drag the red point to set y(x_0) = k_1. Set H = 1 to split the solution into homogeneous plus particular parts.",
    "id": "1"
   },
   {
    "type": "folder",
    "title": "Controls",
    "collapsed": false,
    "id": "2"
   },
